    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-343403",
      "problem": "Consider the function $F(x)=x$ defined on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ The Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼2{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡((2n-1)\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-3}}\nat $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(\\frac{\\pi }{2})={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}}{2n-1}={{field-5}}.\n$$",
